{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm working from the requirement that Style(double_underline=True) should be accepted, which means adding a double_underline keyword. Since underline2 already maps to SGR 21, which is double underline, I'm considering making double_underline an alias for the same bit. That would also make underline2 read as True for that style, and I'm wondering whether that's acceptable since it's semantically the same attribute.\n\nI'm weighing whether to make double_underline a separate keyword that reuses bit 9, or give it its own bit. A separate bit would mean changing the map, so reusing bit 9 looks cleaner. Still, I need the kwarg to be named double_underline so it passes through the attribute mapping, and I'm figuring out how it should sit alongside the existing underline2 argument in __init__.\n\nI'm settling on the implementation: `__init__` gets a `double_underline` parameter, and the flag combines with `underline2` so either one sets bit 9. I'm keeping the `\"underline2\"` string in `__str__` so existing output doesn't change. For `get_html_style`, I'm going to emit `text-decoration: underline double` for that case, though I'm not sure yet how that interacts with the existing separate underline entries.\n\nI'm weighing whether to treat double underline as a plain alias, so the output would reuse the same flag for both. I'm checking how it interacts with the existing underline entry in the HTML export, and I'm considering whether to collect the decorations into one list instead. I'll look at the SVG export at console.py around line 2400 and confirm the markup parser picks up the new attribute and abbreviation.\n\nI'm making double_underline an alias for bit 9 as well, so the keyword is accepted. Next I want to check the `_Bit` descriptor and its definition, then look at the console code around line 2380.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"Plan: SGR 21 is the double-underline code that `underline2` already uses (bit 9). Rather than add a duplicate bit, I'll make `double_underline` a keyword and property that share that bit. Next I'll check the SVG exporter, `_Bit`, and existing tests that pin the `underline2` output."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01JCtGJLeh7xjs7czMyaX3N8","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /app && sed -n 2380,2415p rich/console.py && grep -n \"class _Bit\" -A12 rich/style.py && grep -rn \"underline2\\|uu\" tests/*.py | head -30 && sed -n 1,60p .ki-base/decisions/0003-style-composition-and-ansi.md | head -80"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1509,"cacheRead":12235,"cacheWrite":7650,"totalTokens":21396,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.0007545,"cacheRead":0.00012235,"cacheWrite":0.00095625,"total":0.0018333,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":1250},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1794167642948,"providerThinkingLevel":"medium","responseId":"msg_011Cgr3g4nYzAyHQmeE5pgVp","rawStopReason":"tool_use","durationMs":7965,"thinkingLevel":"medium"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01JCtGJLeh7xjs7czMyaX3N8","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"            css_rules = []\n            color = (\n                _theme.foreground_color\n                if (style.color is None or style.color.is_default)\n                else style.color.get_truecolor(_theme)\n            )\n            bgcolor = (\n                _theme.background_color\n                if (style.bgcolor is None or style.bgcolor.is_default)\n                else style.bgcolor.get_truecolor(_theme)\n            )\n            if style.reverse:\n                color, bgcolor = bgcolor, color\n            if style.dim:\n                color = blend_rgb(color, bgcolor, 0.4)\n            css_rules.append(